  "hints": [
    "The limiter has to see every request before the API does. Which component sits at the front door and can say no cheaply?",
    "Counters need a fast shared store that every API replica can increment: an in-memory cache.",
    "Application Gateway (2) → API (24) → Redis (2) → NoSQL (3)."
  ],
  "scoring": {
    "weights": {
      "performance": 0.35,
      "reliability": 0.3,
      "cost": 0.15,
      "architecture": 0.2
    },
    "latencyTargetMs": 40,
    "costBudget": 2800
  },
  "explanation": [
    "Rate limit at the edge: an Application Gateway authenticates the key and enforces the quota before the request costs you anything.",
    "Token bucket or sliding window counters live in Redis so every replica shares them; increments are O(1) and sub-millisecond.",
    "Run the limiter redundantly. If it's a single box, a limiter outage is a full API outage."
  ]
